  <section class="prose">
    <h1>About Me</h1>
    <p>I'm Harry, a Technical Project Manager based in Toronto. At Stryker, I lead hospital software implementations from scope through go-live, coordinating Engineering, Product, vendors, and clinical/IT teams around integrations, validation, and delivery risks.</p>
    <p>Previously, at Holland Bloorview Kids Rehabilitation Hospital, I led an Agile team building an ML gait-analysis app, coordinated cloud-based model development, and introduced digital prosthetic workflows that reduced production lead time by 30%. That experience shaped how I connect technical decisions to the needs of the people using a system.</p>
    <h2>How I work</h2>
    <p>I start by clarifying the problem, identifying constraints, and defining a manageable scope. I translate technical dependencies into execution plans and work with stakeholders to surface risks early. My personal projects extend that practice: the triage assistant explores AI boundaries and human oversight, Patient Logger explores access control, and this portfolio explores repeatable cloud delivery.</p>
    <p>I'm interested in technical project management opportunities across healthcare technology, cloud platforms, and applied AI. Outside work, I follow the NBA and Formula 1, travel, and search for great local street food.</p>
